ites; SDK CLI health validate and repair contracts carry the distinction; focused cross-version packed-consumer and exact repository coverage gates pass"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-o2kc"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"critical"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"critical"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"Global pm 2026.8.23 writes trackers read by repository-pinned 2026.8.20 and 2026.8.21 binaries"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Create and mutate an item with pm 2026.8.23, run pinned health --strict-exit, compare item_hash_version and hashes, run pinned history-repair, then compare changed receipt, bytes, and both readers' verdicts."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Supported readers attribute incompatible persisted hash capabilities as version skew, and repair never reports a no-op when bytes changed."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Three repositories reproduced opposite integrity verdicts while both writers stamped item_hash_version 2; pinned repair rewrote the stream despite changed=false and inverted which reader accepted it."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"history hashing, drift diagnostics, and repair receipts"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/regression","value":true},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/customer_impact","value":"Ordinary cross-version mutations make CI report corruption, train operators to normalize real integrity alarms away, and hide evidence-rewriting repairs behind a false no-change receipt."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-0wfdim","kind":"recurs_from","created_at":"2026-08-28T08:13:08.155Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-igdvfq","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-28T08:13:08.155Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cl